{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 501351, "name": "Serena Star", "username": "starcross", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/starcross/{size}/53010_2.png", "created_at": "2026-05-09T05:11:16.073Z", "cooked": "<p>Hi all. I’m on Fedora 44 and I just rebooted my computer to see a red update icon in my tray. Upon attempting to run the update in Discover, it threatens to remove “kmod-nvidia-”. I do not see any Nvidia updates pending in the update list. This makes me think that, if I approve this update, I will not have Nvidia drivers installed upon the next boot. I’m curious if this is a bug. I will <em>not</em> approve pending updates and would probably advise others with this problem not do so either.</p>\n<p>Supplemental data:<br>\n<div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/0/c/0cfef240c9d3a1da2a14eb833f6eac9dd05eb521.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/1QXWSaD3dh2yZQhDwMU46VrddlL.png?dl=1\" title=\"image\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"><img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/optimized/3X/0/c/0cfef240c9d3a1da2a14eb833f6eac9dd05eb521_2_261x500.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"1QXWSaD3dh2yZQhDwMU46VrddlL\" width=\"261\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/optimized/3X/0/c/0cfef240c9d3a1da2a14eb833f6eac9dd05eb521_2_261x500.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/0/c/0cfef240c9d3a1da2a14eb833f6eac9dd05eb521.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/0/c/0cfef240c9d3a1da2a14eb833f6eac9dd05eb521.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"51596A\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">338×647 56.9 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 6, "updated_at": "2026-05-09T05:11:16.073Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 803, "reads": 46, "readers_count": 45, "score": 4009.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 190903, "topic_slug": "nvidia-drivers-threatening-to-be-uninstalled-with-kernel-v7-update-possible-bug", "display_username": "Serena Star", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 32474, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/nvidia-drivers-threatening-to-be-uninstalled-with-kernel-v7-update-possible-bug/190903/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 501358, "name": "Leigh Scott", "username": "leigh123linux", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/leigh123linux/{size}/45562_2.png", "created_at": "2026-05-09T05:56:05.553Z", "cooked": "<p>Why don’t you use dnf cli instead of that garbage gui, it seems confusing.</p>\n<p>FTR it’s normal for kmod-nvidia-{old-kernel}  to be removed on kernel update, if you didn’t use the lame gui you would have seen the complete transaction clearly.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 6, "updated_at": "2026-05-09T05:56:05.553Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 12, "reads": 40, "readers_count": 39, "score": 73.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 190903, "topic_slug": "nvidia-drivers-threatening-to-be-uninstalled-with-kernel-v7-update-possible-bug", "display_username": "Leigh Scott", "primary_group_name": "packager", "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Packager Sponsor", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 10536, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/nvidia-drivers-threatening-to-be-uninstalled-with-kernel-v7-update-possible-bug/190903/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 501363, "name": "Serena Star", "username": "starcross", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/starcross/{size}/53010_2.png", "created_at": "2026-05-09T06:24:20.098Z", "cooked": "<p>I tried CLI DNF as well, I can see it removes kmod-nvidia but doesn’t have any mention of a new nvidia package. Or is this just a matter of, updating to Kernel 7 will re-create kmod for the new version?</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 6, "updated_at": "2026-05-09T06:24:20.098Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 10, "reads": 40, "readers_count": 39, "score": 63.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 190903, "topic_slug": "nvidia-drivers-threatening-to-be-uninstalled-with-kernel-v7-update-possible-bug", "display_username": "Serena Star", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 10536, "username": "leigh123linux", "name": "Leigh Scott", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/leigh123linux/{size}/45562_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 32474, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/nvidia-drivers-threatening-to-be-uninstalled-with-kernel-v7-update-possible-bug/190903/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 501364, "name": "Leigh Scott", "username": "leigh123linux", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/leigh123linux/{size}/45562_2.png", "created_at": "2026-05-09T06:27:04.565Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"starcross\" data-display-name=\"Serena Star\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"190903\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/starcross/48/53010_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Serena Star:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Or is this just a matter of, updating to Kernel 7 will re-create kmod for the new version?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes….</p>"